{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.10.6","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-09-13T22:02:55.541Z","id":"af157289-8d48-4085-95f9-ac3558d68b04","content":[{"text":"To make your shadcn registry browsable at `/r/` without interfering with CLI consumers fetching `/r/*.json`, you have three main patterns.\n\n---\n\n### How VitePress \u0026 Static Serving Work Here\n\nCurrently, `docs/scripts/generate-registry.ts` emits JSON manifests to `docs/public/r/`:\n* `https://pantoken.app/r/registry.json`\n* `https://pantoken.app/r/[item].json` (e.g. `button.json`, `theme-canvas.json`, `use-instui-modal.json`)\n\nVitePress serves `docs/public/` files at the root. Requests ending in `.json` will always serve the static file. To make human browser visits to `/r/` display a UI, you can provide an HTML route for `/r/`.\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Interactive Registry Browser (Recommended)\n\nFollow the pattern used by pantoken's other pickers ([docs/guide/cdn-picker.md](docs/guide/cdn-picker.md), [IconPicker.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/IconPicker.vue), [InteractionsPicker.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/InteractionsPicker.vue)):\n\n1. **Create the page** at [docs/r/index.md](docs/r/index.md) (or `docs/guide/registry.md` with a redirect/alias):\n   ```markdown\n   ---\n   title: Registry\n   description: Browse pantoken themes, components, and hooks compatible with shadcn/ui.\n   aside: false\n   editLink: false\n   ---\n\n   \u003cRegistryBrowser /\u003e\n   ```\n\n2. **Create the Vue component** at `docs/.vitepress/theme/components/RegistryBrowser.vue`:\n   - Fetches or imports `/r/registry.json`\n   - Filter tabs: **All**, **Themes** (`registry:theme`), **Hooks** (`registry:hook`), **UI Components** (`registry:ui`)\n   - Search bar to filter by name/description\n   - Copyable CLI install command toggle (`npx shadcn@latest add https://pantoken.app/r/\u003cname\u003e.json`, `pnpm dlx`, `bunx`)\n   - Links to view the raw JSON manifest and corresponding docs\n\n3. **Register the component** in [docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts):\n   ```ts\n   import RegistryBrowser from \"./components/RegistryBrowser.vue\";\n\n   export default {\n     ...Theme,\n     enhanceApp({ app }) {\n       app.component(\"RegistryBrowser\", RegistryBrowser);\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Auto-Generated Markdown Catalog\n\nIf you prefer static documentation pages generated during build time:\n\n1. Update `docs/scripts/generate-registry.ts` to also emit [docs/r/index.md](docs/r/index.md) containing a markdown table / cards of all items, installation commands, and links to each `.json` file.\n2. Add `docs/r/` to `docs/.vitepress/config.ts` nav/sidebar if desired.\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Static HTML Index or Redirect in `public/r/`\n\nIf you only want a minimal directory viewer or redirect when hitting `/r/`:\n\n* **Option 3A (Redirect to `registry.json`):**\n  Add `docs/public/r/index.html` with `\u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; url=/r/registry.json\"\u003e`.\n* **Option 3B (Standalone HTML catalog):**\n  Emit a standalone `docs/public/r/index.html` inside `generate-registry.ts` with lightweight CSS styling listing all available endpoints.\n\n---\n\n### Recommendation\n\n**Option 1** is recommended because it matches the styling of the rest of the pantoken documentation site, lets users preview component metadata, and gives them copy-paste CLI commands for adding components to their apps.","type":"text"}]}
{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.10.6","type":"user","ts":"2026-09-13T22:03:33.465Z","content":[{"text":"option 1."}]}
